Miroku (neutral male monk, and yup, I'm an anime dork) gets to
Minetown, with just enough swag to get himself a protection donation at
level 2.  After donation, he had 7 zorks left - not that I actually
noticed.

Mistake 1: Went into the delicatessen and, seeing a potion, decided to
drink it for IDing purposes. (I tend to drink potions upon discovery -
the only really permanently bad choice is Polymorph, and I rarely come
across that one before I can recover from it without too much
difficulty.)  Went to pay him... oh wait, 7 zorkmids.  Crap.

Luckily (heh) I had bought a wand of polymorph in a dungeon store, so
even if the shopkeeper wouldn't accept any food item I dropped as
payment, I could still somehow plow my way out.  It took four zaps at
the shopkeeper before he turned into something I could tolerate - a
gray ooze.

Mistake 2: Confident he wouldn't bug me after being blob-ified, I
decided not to kill him, opened the door and strode out.

Which called down the biggest horde of Keystone Kops I'd ever seen in
all my games.

A word of precaution to all who ID potions and scrolls just by reading
them - buy them first, THEN use them. (*cue "The More You Know" music*)


